your Johnson &amp; Johnson?

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did. I was --

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
I had, like, a --

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:08.688
Not that I -- I didn't cry
I got a little, like, misty.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, at least
that part is done.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I was like --
It was so weird.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.728 line:92%
I just didn't know how to speak.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:18.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Thank you for helping us!

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Which is like --

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.071 line:92%
-I'm so glad you said that

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.373 line:92%
-Yeah, it was like -- You know

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, you know,
it's like FEMA.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.277 line:92%
They came in and saved the city!

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was like,
"Thank you for helping us!

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:37.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What did you --
When you were a chemist, did -

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
did the other people in the la
have any idea

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:44.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
that comedy was in your future
or even a talent of yours?

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:44.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
